{
    "background_story": "Jaxon was a talented musician who had always dreamed of making it big. After years of struggling to make ends meet, he finally landed a record deal with a major label. However, the pressures of fame and the constant scrutiny took a toll on his mental health. Jaxon felt suffocated by the expectations of his management team and the constant need to produce hits. He began to feel like a puppet on strings, losing control over his own music and artistry. The fame and fortune he once craved now felt hollow, and Jaxon couldn't shake off the feeling of unhappiness that had settled in his heart. He started to question whether the price of success was worth the cost of his own happiness and creative freedom.",
